{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>It came to pass.</b> The manna came down more than usual, as he will explain, \"and Israel gathered a double portion of bread,\" for Moses had commanded them to do so, and they did not know why. Furthermore, Scripture says לָקְטוּ (they gathered) and does not say מָצְאוּ (they found), and the princes came and told Moses that Israel had done as he commanded them, and they asked him what they should do — why did he command to gather a double portion, and how could they eat it?"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:08.476335422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}